From: Yocto build fix
Subject: [PATCH] autoapp: match input geometry to what's actually rendered

InputDevice scales touch coordinates from touchscreenGeometry_ into
displayGeometry_ (the negotiated Android Auto video resolution) --
see InputDevice::handleTouchEvent(). touchscreenGeometry_ was being
set from QGuiApplication::primaryScreen()->geometry(), i.e. the full
1280x720 this board's HDMI scanout is forced to. But the physical
panel only ever displays roughly the first 1024x600 of that frame
(see the paired QtVideoOutput.cpp change), so touch coordinates were
being scaled against a canvas larger than what's actually shown,
misplacing every touch relative to the content on screen.

Use the exact same real-panel geometry here that QtVideoOutput now
renders into (kPanelVisibleGeometry there), rather than the full
screen. This also happens to exactly match this panel's own
touchscreen hardware calibration range (Qt's evdevtouch log reports
"min X: 0 max X: 1024", "min Y: 0 max Y: 600" for this device), making
the transform a clean 1:1 identity mapping instead of a scaled one.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe-specific: this board's HDMI scanout
resolution and its physical panel's real visible resolution are
different, which upstream has no reason to account for]

diff --git a/src/autoapp/Service/ServiceFactory.cpp b/src/autoapp/Service/ServiceFactory.cpp
index 5f9d60e..d52842c 100644
--- a/src/autoapp/Service/ServiceFactory.cpp
+++ b/src/autoapp/Service/ServiceFactory.cpp
@@ -120,8 +120,17 @@ IService::Pointer ServiceFactory::createInputService(aasdk::messenger::IMessenge
         break;
     }
 
-    QScreen* screen = QGuiApplication::primaryScreen();
-    QRect screenGeometry = screen == nullptr ? QRect(0, 0, 1, 1) : screen->geometry();
+    // screenGeometry here must match the area QtVideoOutput actually renders
+    // into (see kPanelVisibleGeometry in QtVideoOutput.cpp), NOT the full
+    // primaryScreen()->geometry() -- this board's HDMI scanout (1280x720) is
+    // larger than the physical panel's real visible/native area (1024x600),
+    // so using the full screen here would scale touch coordinates onto a
+    // canvas bigger than what's actually shown, misplacing every touch.
+    // 1024x600 also happens to be this exact panel's own touchscreen
+    // hardware calibration range (confirmed via Qt's evdevtouch device
+    // discovery log: "min X: 0 max X: 1024", "min Y: 0 max Y: 600"), so this
+    // makes the touch transform a clean 1:1 identity mapping.
+    QRect screenGeometry(0, 0, 1024, 600);
     projection::IInputDevice::Pointer inputDevice(std::make_shared<projection::InputDevice>(*QApplication::instance(), configuration_, std::move(screenGeometry), std::move(videoGeometry)));
 
     return std::make_shared<InputService>(ioService_, messenger, std::move(inputDevice));
